{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3275","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-provider-neutral-cache-bypass.md@sha256:d36d4de33aef52faf064f6b434e199f72e68ad365d7709ae711aab09c8c6aff4"},"owner_reference":"3275","content":"# Architecture Spec: Provider-Neutral Cache-Bypass Option for backlog_list / backlog_view\n\nBacklog item: #3275\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nTwo changes to the backlog MCP+CLI surface, both reusing existing reconciliation code with zero\nnew reconciliation logic:\n\n1. **Rename** `backlog_list`'s GitHub-specific `from_github` parameter to the provider-neutral\n   `refresh` \u2014 on the MCP tool, on `operations.list_items()`'s own kwarg, and on the sole internal\n   caller (`sam_schema/backlog.py:95`). CLI `list --refresh` is unaffected (already neutral).\n2. **Add** a `refresh: bool = False` parameter to `backlog_view` (MCP) and CLI `view`, threaded\n   into `operations.view_item()`. When `True`, it forces a live-backend check through the already-shared\n   `view_enrich_from_github()` \u2192 `work_item_version()` resolution chain \u2014 the same head-pointer/\n   audit-comment resolver the write/reconcile path uses \u2014 for **both** numeric/`#N`/URL selectors\n   and title-substring selectors that already resolved locally. This closes the actual gap: today\n   only numeric selectors ever get a live check, and only unconditionally (no way to skip it), while\n   title selectors that resolve locally never do.\n\n`backlog_list_followups`/CLI `list-followups` are **out of scope**, per the item's own Acceptance\nCriteria (see \u00a710 ADR-4).\n\n## 2. Architecture Overview\n\n```mermaid\nC4Context\n    title Cache-bypass capability \u2014 system context\n    Person(caller, \"MCP client / CLI user\", \"Agent or human verifying synced state\")\n    System(backlog, \"backlog_core\", \"MCP server + CLI, cache + reconciliation\")\n    System_Ext(github, \"GitHub Issues API\", \"Authoritative backend (one of several)\")\n    Rel(caller, backlog, \"backlog_view(refresh=true) / view --refresh\")\n    Rel(backlog, github, \"view_enrich_from_github() \u2192 work_item_version()\", \"HTTPS\")\n```\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    subgraph \"MCP surface (server.py)\"\n        BL[\"backlog_list(refresh: bool)\"]\n        BV[\"backlog_view(refresh: bool)\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"CLI surface (sam_schema/backlog.py)\"\n        CL[\"list --refresh\"]\n        CV[\"view --refresh\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"Orchestration (operations.py)\"\n        LI[\"list_items(refresh: bool)\"]\n        VI[\"view_item(refresh: bool)\"]\n        RC[\"refresh_local_cache_from_github()\"]\n    end\n    subgraph \"GitHub resolution chain (unchanged, reused)\"\n        VE1[\"GitHubBackend.view_enrich_from_github()<br/>backends/github_backend.py:546\"]\n        VE2[\"gh_client.view_enrich_from_github()<br/>gh_client.py:1716\"]\n        WIV[\"GitHubWorkItems.work_item_version()<br/>backends/github_work_items.py:341\"]\n    end\n    BL --> LI\n    CL --> LI\n    BV --> VI\n    CV --> VI\n    LI -->|refresh=True| RC\n    VI -->|refresh=True, or no local copy| VE1\n    VE1 --> VE2\n    VE2 -->|resolve_version callback| WIV\n```\n\nNo new modules, no new services, no new reconciliation entry points. The change is parameter\nplumbing plus one control-flow restructure in `view_item()` (\u00a74.3).\n\n## 3. Technology Stack\n\nNo new dependencies. Uses existing FastMCP `Annotated[bool, Field(...)]` tool-parameter pattern\n(already used by `from_github`/`full_refresh`) and existing Typer `Annotated[bool, typer.Option(...)]`\nCLI pattern (already used by `--refresh`/`--full-refresh`).\n\n## 4. Component Design\n\n### 4.1 MCP `backlog_list` (server.py:1935)\n\nRename the parameter in place \u2014 no new capability, pure rename:\n\n```python\nasync def backlog_list(\n    refresh: Annotated[\n        bool,\n        Field(description=\"Refresh the local cache from the configured backend before listing\"),\n    ] = False,\n    ...  # all other existing params unchanged\n) -> dict:\n```\n\n- server.py:2104 docstring: `\"Use from_github=true...\"` \u2192 `\"Use refresh=true to refresh the local cache from the backend before listing.\"`\n- server.py:2143 forwarding call: `from_github=from_github` \u2192 `refresh=refresh`\n\n### 4.2 `operations.list_items()` (operations.py:1766-1807)\n\n```python\ndef list_items(\n    refresh: bool = False,\n    ...  # unchanged\n) -> dict[str, int | list[str] | list[dict[str, str | bool]]]:\n```\n\nBody change: `if from_github:` \u2192 `if refresh:` (operations.py:1806). Docstring's `from_github` arg\ndescription renamed to `refresh` (operations.py:1782).\n\n**Sole caller** `sam_schema/backlog.py:95`: `operations.list_items(from_github=refresh, ...)` \u2192\n`operations.list_items(refresh=refresh, ...)`. The CLI's local variable is already named `refresh`\n(from `--refresh`, line 79-81) \u2014 this rename removes the existing name-mismatch, it doesn't\nintroduce one. No CLI-facing change; `--refresh` stays `--refresh`.\n\n### 4.3 MCP `backlog_view` (server.py:2392) \u2014 new `refresh` parameter\n\nAdd, positioned immediately after `selector` for discoverability:\n\n```python\n    refresh: Annotated[\n        bool,\n        Field(\n            description=(\n                \"Bypass the local cache and validate against the live backend. For GitHub, \"\n                \"resolves content through the authoritative head-pointer/audit-comment record \"\n                \"(never the raw issue body) \u2014 same resolution the write/reconcile path uses. \"\n                \"Applies to every selector shape: a title-substring selector that already \"\n                \"resolves locally gets the same live-check opportunity a numeric/#N/URL \"\n                \"selector does. When False (default), a selector that already resolves to a \"\n                \"local item returns the cached copy without a network call; a selector with no \"\n                \"local match still triggers a live lookup regardless of this flag, since that is \"\n                \"the only way to resolve its identity at all.\"\n            )\n        ),\n    ] = False,\n```\n\nForward it into the `asyncio.to_thread(operations.view_item, ...)` call at server.py:2591-2601 as\n`refresh=refresh`.\n\n### 4.4 `operations.view_item()` (operations.py:2854) \u2014 restructured branching\n\nAdd `refresh: bool = False` to the signature (after `section`). **Behavior change, deliberate**: the\nexisting unconditional live call for numeric/`#N`/URL selectors (today's operations.py:2917-2918)\ncurrently fires on *every* view-by-number call, even when a local cached copy already exists \u2014\nthis is what the grooming research flagged as \"uncontrolled.\" This spec gates that call behind\n`refresh` **only when a local copy already exists**; it is preserved unconditionally when no local\ncopy exists at all, because that path is identity resolution (\"does this item exist anywhere?\"),\nnot cache validation, and must not regress into a false `ItemNotFoundError`.\n\nAdd one small private helper \u2014 the piece every existing call site got right implicitly by only\never being reached with a numeric selector, and that a naive `refresh` implementation would get\nwrong for title selectors (passing a title string into `view_enrich_from_github()` reaches\n`int(issue_num)` in `gh_client.py:1742`, which raises an uncaught `ValueError` \u2014 no `except\nBacklogException` there catches it):\n\n```python\ndef _live_lookup_id(item: BacklogItem | None, issue_num: str | None, selector: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Resolve the identifier to pass to view_enrich_from_github() for a live check.\n\n    Precedence: an already-parsed numeric selector; else the cached item's own\n    known issue number/id (for a title-selector match \u2014 never the raw title\n    text, which the GitHub backend cannot resolve); else the raw selector\n    (bare beads nanoid with no local match yet). Returns None only when no\n    identifier of any kind is resolvable.\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nContract (implementer fills this exact body):\n- `issue_num` truthy \u2192 return it unchanged (existing numeric/#N/URL path).\n- else `item is not None`: return `str(item.number)` if `item.number` is set, else\n  `item.issue.lstrip(\"#\") or None` if `item.issue` is set, else `None`.\n- else (`item is None`): return `selector.strip() or None` (bare nanoid / string-id backends only \u2014\n  callers only reach this branch when `backend.issue_id_type == \"string\"`, per the restructured\n  branching below).\n\nRestructured control flow (replaces operations.py:2912-2933; every existing branch outcome \u2014\ncases A-G below \u2014 is preserved bit-for-bit when `refresh=False`; only the \"item already cached\"\nbranches (A/B) become opt-in, and title-selector cached items (case H, previously dead code) gain\nthe same opt-in live check):\n\n```python\nitem = find_item(get_config().backend.list_work_items(), selector)\nissue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)\nresult: ViewItemResult = view_result_from_local_item(item) if item else ViewItemResult()\n\nif item:\n    if refresh:\n        live_id = _live_lookup_id(item, issue_num, selector)\n        enriched = view_enrich_from_github(result, live_id, repo) if live_id else False\n        if not enriched:\n            out.warnings.append(\n                \"backend unreachable \u2014 sections_index reflects provider-backed record, may be stale\"\n            )\n    result.groomed = item.metadata.groomed\nelif issue_num or get_config().backend.issue_id_type == \"string\":\n    live_id = _live_lookup_id(item, issue_num, selector)\n    enriched = view_enrich_from_github(result, live_id, repo) if live_id else False\n    if not enriched:\n        raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)\nelse:\n    raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)\n```\n\nTruth table verifying no regression (A-G = existing behavior today, H = new capability):\n\n| Case | issue_num | item cached | refresh | Old behavior | New behavior |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | yes | yes | \u2014 | always live-checks, updates `result` in place | live-checks only if `refresh=True` |\n| B | yes | yes, enrich fails | \u2014 | warns, falls back to cache | same, only reached when `refresh=True` |\n| C | yes | no | \u2014 | live discovery, no exception | unchanged (identity-resolution branch) |\n| D | yes | no, enrich fails | \u2014 | raises `ItemNotFoundError` | unchanged |\n| E/F | no (string-id backend) | no | \u2014 | live discovery via nanoid | unchanged |\n| G | no (non-string-id backend) | no | \u2014 | raises `ItemNotFoundError` | unchanged |\n| H | no (title selector) | yes | \u2014 | **no live check possible, ever** | live-checks only if `refresh=True`, via `item.number`/`item.issue`, never the raw title |\n\n### 4.5 CLI `view` (sam_schema/backlog.py:110-124) \u2014 new `--refresh` flag\n\n```python\n@app.command(\"view\")\ndef view(\n    selector: Annotated[str, typer.Option(\"--selector\", help=\"Item selector\")],\n    refresh: Annotated[\n        bool, typer.Option(\"--refresh\", help=\"Bypass the local cache and validate against the live backend\")\n    ] = False,\n    repo: ...,  # unchanged\n    ...\n) -> None:\n    result = operations.view_item(\n        selector=selector, repo=repo, offset=offset, limit=limit, show=show,\n        since=since, output=output, section=section, refresh=refresh,\n    )\n```\n\nSame flag name (`--refresh`) and same underlying parameter name as CLI `list`, closing the naming\ngap the Impact Radius section identified between the two CLI commands.\n\n## 5. Data Architecture\n\nNo new data models. `ViewItemResult` (models.py:1432) and `ViewItemResultCompact` (models.py:1478)\nare unchanged \u2014 the existing `warnings: list[str]` field already carries the\n\"backend unreachable... may be stale\" message pattern this spec reuses for a failed live-check on\n`refresh=True`; no new status/freshness field is added (YAGNI \u2014 nothing in the Acceptance Criteria\nrequires the response to declare whether it was served live vs. cached, only that the option to\nforce live exists and resolves through the authoritative path when used).\n\n## 6. Type System Design\n\nNo new domain identifiers. `refresh: bool` matches the existing `from_github`/`full_refresh`\nboolean convention already established in this codebase \u2014 introducing an enum or `Literal` for a\nsingle on/off cache-bypass toggle would be unrequested abstraction (also consistent with current\nFastMCP tool-design guidance to avoid `Literal`/`Enum` params where a plain type suffices).\n`_live_lookup_id()` is the one new function; its return type `str | None` is deliberate \u2014 `None`\nis a real, reachable state (a cached item with no known backend id at all) and must not be\nsilently coerced to an empty-string call into `view_enrich_from_github()`.\n\nNo boundary-validation changes: `_live_lookup_id()` sits entirely inside the already-typed\ninternal core (operates on `BacklogItem | None`, returns `str | None`); it does not parse untrusted\nexternal input \u2014 `parse_issue_selector()` already owns that boundary and is unchanged.\n\n## 7. Security Architecture\n\nNo new attack surface, no new credentials. `refresh=True` invokes the same authenticated GitHub\nAPI path (`try_get_github()` \u2192 GraphQL fetch) that `from_github`/numeric-selector views already\nuse today unconditionally \u2014 the change narrows when that call fires for already-cached numeric\nitems (fewer live calls by default), and adds it as an explicit opt-in for title selectors and CLI\n`view` (a net-neutral-to-lower blast radius, not an expansion). No secrets are read or logged by\nthis change.\n\n## 8. Testing Architecture\n\n**Rename-affected (update, do not just re-run)** \u2014 change `from_github=` keyword to `refresh=`:\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` lines 450, 712, 735, 758, 780, 797, 844, 868, 894, 1760;\n  rename `test_list_items_from_github_calls_refresh` (784-797) to\n  `test_list_items_refresh_calls_refresh_local_cache`.\n- `tests_backlog/test_reconciliation_wrapper.py:111`.\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_server.py:197,203,206,209` \u2014 rename the MCP-payload dict key\n  `{\"from_github\": True}` to `{\"refresh\": True}`.\n- `tests/test_scenarios.py:116-119, 1516-1517` \u2014 same dict-key rename.\n- `tests/test_live_validation.py:286` (`test_l9_pull_refresh_from_github`) \u2014 verify first: per Wave 0\n  research this exercises the `pull` refresh path, not `list`/`view`. Rename only if it actually\n  references the renamed keyword; otherwise leave it (naming false positive, not this item's scope).\n\n**New tests required** (no existing coverage per Files section audit):\n- `operations.view_item()`: cached item + title selector + `refresh=True` \u2192 `view_enrich_from_github`\n  called with the item's `number`/`issue`-derived id, never the raw title string.\n- `operations.view_item()`: cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` (new default) \u2192\n  `view_enrich_from_github` NOT called (locks in the new default; this is the regression-risk case).\n- `operations.view_item()`: no cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` \u2192 live lookup still\n  fires (regression guard against the false-`ItemNotFoundError` bug this spec explicitly avoids).\n- `operations.view_item()`: no cached item + beads nanoid + `refresh=False` \u2192 live lookup still fires.\n- `operations.view_item()`: cached item + `refresh=True` + item has no resolvable id (`item.number`\n  and `item.issue` both empty) \u2192 warns, does not raise, does not call `view_enrich_from_github`.\n- `server.py` `backlog_view`: `refresh` param forwards into `operations.view_item` call.\n- `sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py`: new file coverage \u2014 CLI `view --refresh` forwards\n  `refresh=True`; CLI `list --refresh` still forwards correctly post-rename (this file currently has\n  no coverage of either command per the Files section audit \u2014 both need tests, not just the new flag).\n\nCoverage target: `operations.py`'s `view_item()`/`list_items()` are business logic (existing repo\nconvention) \u2192 90% minimum on the touched branches per `python3-testing` skill's coverage table.\n\n## 9. Distribution Architecture\n\nNo packaging change. No new PEP 723 dependencies. Changes are confined to existing modules within\nthe `development-harness` plugin already on the distribution path.\n\n## 10. Architectural Decisions (ADRs)\n\n**ADR-1: Shared parameter name is `refresh`, not `full_refresh` or a new coined name.**\n`full_refresh` already carries specific meaning (`ReconcileScope.INITIAL` vs `.INCREMENTAL`,\noperations.py:1599) scoped to `sync_now`/CLI `refresh` \u2014 reusing it for `list`/`view` would\nconflate two different concepts (reconcile granularity vs. per-call cache bypass). `refresh` is\nalready the CLI's established, working, provider-neutral name for `list` (`--refresh`); converging\n`backlog_list`, `backlog_view`, and CLI `view` on it removes the one existing name-mismatch\n(`--refresh` \u2192 `from_github` translation) instead of adding a second one.\n\n**ADR-2: `operations.list_items()`'s own `from_github` kwarg is also renamed \u2014 no deprecation alias.**\nPer Fact-Check claim 6 (VERIFIED): the sole production caller is `sam_schema/backlog.py:95`, a\nsingle internal call site within the same plugin, not a published external API. Standard Python\ndeprecation-alias practice (decorator-based warning + forwarding) exists for cases where external\ncallers can't be updated atomically; that condition does not hold here \u2014 updating the one caller in\nthe same change is strictly simpler and leaves no stale alias to remove later.\n\n**ADR-3: The numeric-selector unconditional live call is gated behind `refresh` only when a local\ncopy already exists; identity-resolution live calls (no local copy) stay unconditional.**\nConfirmed via a full case-by-case trace (\u00a74.4 truth table) against existing tests \u2014 no test in\n`tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` asserts the previously-unconditional numeric-selector live\ncall for an *already-cached* item, so no test regression. Ungated identity-resolution (cases C-G)\nis preserved exactly, because gating it would turn \"item not yet synced\" into a false\n`ItemNotFoundError` \u2014 a correctness regression, not a cache-bypass feature.\n\n**ADR-4: `backlog_list_followups`/CLI `list-followups` are deferred, not included.**\nThe item's own groomed Acceptance Criteria and Expected Behavior sections name only\n`backlog_list`/CLI `list` and `backlog_view`/CLI `view` \u2014 `list_followups` is absent from both.\nImpact Radius flagged it as \"same structural gap... planner decision, include or explicitly defer\";\nthe Acceptance Criteria is the resolved decision (deferred). Recommend filing a follow-up backlog\nitem for `backlog_list_followups`/CLI `list-followups` referencing this item's `refresh` convention\nonce #3275 ships, rather than expanding this item's already-large blast radius further (Grooming\nNotes: feasibility gate was already BLOCKED once on scope size and required explicit user\nconfirmation to proceed at the current MCP+CLI scope).\n\n**ADR-5: No new reconciliation code.** `view_enrich_from_github()` (backends/github_backend.py:546\n\u2192 gh_client.py:1716) and `GitHubWorkItems.work_item_version()` (backends/github_work_items.py:341)\nare reused exactly as they exist today, called from one additional site (\u00a74.4) with one new\nresolvable-id helper (`_live_lookup_id`). No changes to `backend_types.py`'s `SyncProvider`\nprotocol, to `reconcile()`, or to any backend's `view_enrich_from_github()` implementation\n(github/beads/memory/sqlite backends, all sharing the identical `(result, issue_num: str, repo) ->\nbool` signature \u2014 confirmed by grep across all four backend files).\n\n## 11. Scalability Strategy\n\nNo new concurrency pattern. The live-check call is synchronous Python already wrapped in\n`asyncio.to_thread()` at the MCP boundary (server.py:2591, unchanged) \u2014 the same pattern\n`backlog_list`'s `from_github` path already uses. `refresh=True` on `backlog_view`/CLI `view` adds\nat most one network round-trip per call, identical in cost to today's unconditional numeric-selector\npath; gating it behind an explicit flag for already-cached items (ADR-3) reduces average network\ncall volume relative to today's behavior, it does not increase it.\n\n## Documentation Updates (required, not optional \u2014 Acceptance Criteria item 6)\n\n- `skills/backlog/SKILL.md:54` \u2014 parameter table row: `from_github` \u2192 `refresh`.\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:224` \u2014 usage example: `from_github=False,  # refresh local cache from GitHub first` \u2192 `refresh=False,  # refresh local cache from the backend first`.\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:253, 283` \u2014 prose referencing `from_github` \u2192 `refresh`.\n- `skills/backlog/README.md:322-337` (`backlog_view` usage example) \u2014 extend with the new `refresh`\n  parameter and CLI `--refresh` flag example.\n- Generated docs (`docs/dh-workflow-graph.json`, `docs/workflow-layers/G8-backend-routing.json`,\n  `graphify-out/graph.json`) \u2014 do not hand-edit; regenerate via `dh:meta-workflow-graph-refresh`\n  and the `graphify` skill after the code/doc change lands.\n"}